Package: python3-dbus-testing
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 python3,
 python3-dbus,
 python3-gi,
 python3-yaml,
 dbus-daemon | dbus,
Recommends: python3-dbusmock
Suggests: dbus-testing-dsm-host
Description: Configuration-driven DBus interface test framework for DDE
 dbus-testing runs interface tests against freshly built binaries on a private
 D-Bus, driven by YAML only: no glue code and no changes to the code under test.
 .
 It talks to the service under test through the bus alone, so the service may be
 written in any language. Test cases are six primitives (call, get-prop,
 set-prop, wait-signal, check-contract, mock-state) and five assertions
 (signature, value, type, error, nonempty); reports are emitted as JUnit XML,
 JSON and a single-file HTML page.
 .
 Install python3-dbusmock to isolate services that need mocked dependencies.

Package: dbus-testing-dsm-host
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Enhances: python3-dbus-testing
Description: Optional DSM plugin host stand-in for dbus-testing
 A minimal Qt-based host that dlopen()s a deepin-service-manager plugin and
 calls its DSMRegister() entry point on a caller-supplied bus address, because
 deepin-service-manager itself resolves its plugin config directory at compile
 time and cannot be pointed at a build tree.
 .
 This is the only non-Python component of the framework; it is packaged
 separately and only needed for "kind: dsm" services. When it is not installed,
 dbus-testing degrades those services to "mode: attach".
 .
 Verified against the real dde-appearance DSM plugin: it handles both the
 canonical style (the host registers the bus name) and the common style where
 the plugin registers the name itself through QDBusConnection::sessionBus().
